{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:ee651ed2be4a42bf","name":"Sith Warbird","source":{"id":"source:reference-ee651ed2be4a42bf","title":"Sith Warbird","revision":20536,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T00:02:27Z","sha256":"9c5fdbc5348c2cfcdd1d20d8f4f248a41d15b7862ab6edd24257dc5807775104","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=20536","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Sith%20Warbird&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-ee651ed2be4a42bf","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi Academy Training Manual"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi_Academy_Training_Manual"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Sith"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Sith","referenceId":"reference:32bde5e69837ac8e"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Sith Warbird is just one of the many domesticated creatures pressed into military service. Instead of wings, the Sith Warbird has two small arms ending in claws. Its hide is remarkably thick, capable of having hooks or spikes securely embedded without harming the beast. The Sith Warbird relies on its massive size to ram and trample prey, although it can also gore enemies to death with its huge, blunt beak.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Sith Warbirds are notoriously bad-tempered and prone to attack nearly any perceived threats. ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Sith"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Sith","referenceId":"reference:32bde5e69837ac8e"}," would mount specially designed ",{"tag":"a","children":["Sith Battle Harnesses"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sith_Battle_Harnesses"}," to these creatures, providing protection for the rider and allowing the Warbird to carry a powerful weapon, typically a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Blaster Cannon"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Blaster_Cannon","referenceId":"reference:ae1584087cb7657b"},". ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Sith"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Sith","referenceId":"reference:32bde5e69837ac8e"}," would then deploy these mobile weapons platforms at the front of infantry assaults, using them to soften up enemy targets.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Sith Warbird Encounters"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Sith Warbirds were common sights during ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Great Sith War"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Great_Sith_War"},", around 4,000 years before the Battle of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Yavin"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Yavin"},". Their primary purpose was to spearhead assaults, providing heavy firepower for accompanying infantry, Sith Warbirds were also used for scouting missions and reconnaissance, as living creatures are less likely to show up on detection devices. Sith Warbirds still exist in other ",{"tag":"a","children":["Eras of Play"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Eras_of_Play","referenceId":"reference:8e95f83b34b3926d"},", with survivors breeding on planets that once hosted long-forgotten battles and terrorizing local fauna that poses no threat to them.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Sith Warbird Statistics (CL 7)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Huge ",{"tag":"a","children":["Beast"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Beast","referenceId":"reference:628bf77a740094a9"}," 8\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +5; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +9\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 23 (",{"tag":"a","